In the recorded reference run, all three implementations agree for all six
settings. They spend 6-25 evaluations per run. Final fitness ranges from about
0.4898 to 0.7086; none classifies all four XOR cases correctly. This is a small
mechanism test, and its limited search budget does not solve the benchmark.

**Figure fig_10_02. Accepted fitness versus evaluations actually spent.**
Only the Nx traces are drawn; the assertions compare all implementations.
The horizontal axis includes the initial evaluation.

